{"question": "During Winter Storm Uri, what was the highest real-time price at the ERCOT hub average?", "grid": "ercot", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "today": "2026-10-04", "retried": true, "first_violations": ["15"], "request_ids": ["req_011Cfgq7MN921GPZ6WXnRSLx", "req_011Cfgq7VZkSwn7WMTVotRdZ", "req_011Cfgq7atUozfLqp5fXf6nB", "req_011Cfgq7oHrc2p6gFBPjZzsF", "req_011Cfgq7weeRYjZwoiUpCiLH", "req_011Cfgq87idPed9Ed5jpudBB", "req_011Cfgq8GA8ijEHprXCpYE1G", "req_011Cfgq8Tfg9Z3HSwQdKuvrx", "req_011Cfgq8cPYhq8i7emTK3tKy", "req_011Cfgq8srU9aPv7REDWjPkf"], "first_answer": "The highest 15-minute real-time price at the ERCOT hub average (HB_HUBAVG) in February 2021, the month of Winter Storm Uri, was 9051.55 USD/MWh (ercot_peak_premium_monthly, variable all_max, derived table). This is the maximum over the whole calendar month (2688 fifteen-minute intervals), not only the Uri days. This chat cannot read the Uri-specific event table, so I could not isolate the Uri window. The months on either side peaked far lower: January 2021 at 703.62 USD/MWh and March 2021 at 768.64 USD/MWh (same table), so the February maximum almost certainly falls in the storm. The table's dates are UTC month labels, and the months are local America/Chicago months.", "status": "answered", "answer": "The highest real-time price at the ERCOT hub average (HB_HUBAVG) in February 2021, the month of Winter Storm Uri, was 9051.55 USD/MWh (ercot_peak_premium_monthly, variable all_max, derived table). This is the maximum over the whole calendar month, which holds 2688 real-time intervals, not only the Uri days. This chat cannot read the Uri-specific event table, so I could not isolate the Uri window. The months on either side peaked far lower: January 2021 at 703.62 USD/MWh and March 2021 at 768.64 USD/MWh (same table), so the February maximum almost certainly falls in the storm. The table labels months by UTC date, and the months are local America/Chicago months.", "citations": [{"table": "ercot_peak_premium_m