{"question": "How has ERCOT's operating battery fleet grown year by year since 2020? Give the MW at the end of 2020 and of 2025.", "grid": "ercot", "model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "today": "2026-10-04", "retried": false, "first_violations": [], "request_ids": ["req_011CfgqC5dDxTfPHECThJXH2", "req_011CfgqCDMpZdF85NKotJSwq", "req_011CfgqCLBq94Z8EpuVgVe2w", "req_011CfgqCSMubEEekiXCMxXEC", "req_011CfgqCajS9rg5XH8erucCp", "req_011CfgqDAQFTdHnJcanPvTNq"], "status": "answered", "answer": "ERCOT's operating battery fleet was 218.4 MW at the end of 2020 and 13909.3 MW at the end of 2025 (storage_capacity, derived from EIA-860M, August 2026 vintage). Both are sums of nameplate MW for units with status operating whose operating date falls before 2021-01-01 and 2026-01-01 (UTC). Units retired before the vintage are not in this table, so earlier year-ends may be understated.\n\nCapacity added by units that came online in each year (MW, storage_capacity, derived):\n- 2020: 111.2\n- 2021: 602.5\n- 2022: 1309.1\n- 2023: 2043.5\n- 2024: 4120.3\n- 2025: 5615.5\n- 2026 so far: 4295.2, from 55 units (partial year)\n\nAdditions rose every year, and 2025 added the most of any full year.", "citations": [{"table": "storage_capacity", "source_report": "erw:storage_capacity", "data_version": "local backend, data commit de240aa799cc; table last run 2026-09-29T23:58:50Z", "tier": "derived"}], "not_in_warehouse": false, "tool_calls": 8, "calls": [{"tool": "list_tables", "input": {"iso": "ERCOT", "sector": "power"}, "is_error": false, "result_chars": 5818}, {"tool": "describe_table", "input": {"table": "storage_buildout_monthly"}, "is_error": true, "result_chars": 109}, {"tool": "list_tables", "input": {"iso": "ERCOT"}, "is_error": false, "result_chars": 5818}, {"tool": "describe_table", "input": {"table": "storage_capacity"}, "is_error": false, "result_chars": 3116}, {"tool": "describe_table", "input": {"table": "eia860m_operating_generators"}, "is_error": true, "result_chars": 113}, {"tool": "qu